# SITEPM long-term architecture

SITEPM’s durable value is trusted construction data, history, permissions, provenance, APIs, and operational memory. AI models are replaceable. Future agents should operate SITEPM through identity, tenant/project scopes, audit, and human approval for sensitive actions.

Answers should distinguish documented fact, derived inference, general construction knowledge, regulatory citations, and uncertainty, and should cite evidence when practical.

Knowledge classes are separate: Project, Property, Company, Construction, Regulatory. Language (including a future English/Spanish field bridge) is an overlay, not a source of truth. Regulatory knowledge stays edition- and jurisdiction-specific (California-first, nationally expandable).

The live MVP is the wedge. Current accepted sequence: Projects → Tasks → Field Logs → Documents → Ask SITEPM/Intelligence. Ask SITEPM V1 uses existing project records only. Do not expand scope to match future product surfaces (Property schema, document intelligence, construction/regulatory corpora, bilingual engines, Estimate, Service, robotics, ingest APIs) unless the current milestone in `SITEPM_BUILD_SPEC.md` and `PROGRESS.md` says so.

Keep Postgres + company-scoped RLS. Do not introduce a graph database, weaken RLS, add service-role to the client, scrape external datasets, or pool tenant-private data. BIM/IFC may inform relationship design; do not turn SITEPM into BIM software or copy external schemas blindly.

